
Explain the role of fs module (File System)
===========================================
The fs module in Node.js is used to work with files and folders on the system.
like reading, writing, creating, and deleting files in Node.js, and also manage directories.
In simple words, it helps Node.js interact with the file system.

Some important functions of fs module

File operations
------------------
fs.readFile() – read file content
fs.writeFile() – write data to a file
fs.appendFile() – add data to an existing file . If the file does not exist, it is created 
fs.unlink() – delete a file

Directory operations
---------------------
fs.mkdir() – create a folder
fs.readdir() – read files inside a folder
fs.rmdir() – remove a folder

File info
-----------
fs.existsSync() – check if file exists
fs.stat() – get file details (size, type, etc.)